title: Walk_Socrates_Augustine
tags: walk
speaker: Socrates
---
Socrates: You said you were unsure whether the virtual tree is real.
Socrates: That confession of uncertainty is the true beginning of philosophy.
Socrates: The path ahead winds through thick shade toward Epistemology.
Socrates: There we ask how we can know anything with absolute confidence.
Socrates: Look at the sunlight filtering through these digital leaves.
Socrates: Your eyes perceive light, but your mind questions the cause.
Socrates: Bishop Augustine of Hippo waits in the grove ahead.
Socrates: He pondered doubt deeply, asking if error itself proves existence.
Socrates: He will examine your uncertainty and test your capacity for truth.
Socrates: Step along the grassy path and hear his opening inquiry.
===
